# Line endings that do not depend on the machine doing the checkout.
#
# A Windows runner checks out with core.autocrlf=true, which writes CRLF.
# ci.yml's Windows test job and release.yml's windows-x86_64 leg both run
# .github/scripts/smoke.sh under Git Bash, and bash cannot run it with CRLF
# endings: `set -euo pipefail` arrives as `pipefail\r`, an option that does
# not exist, and the script exits 2 before it has checked anything.
#
# The TOML parser accepts CRLF, but smoke.sh lints examples/markdoc-lint.toml
# verbatim, so that file is held to the same bytes on every runner too.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
